{"id":4320,"date":"2024-08-02T10:29:59","date_gmt":"2024-08-02T09:29:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4320"},"modified":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","modified_gmt":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","slug":"ccac-recognised-in-coppermill-primary-school-ofsted-report","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/ccac-recognised-in-coppermill-primary-school-ofsted-report\/","title":{"rendered":"CCAC recognised in Coppermill Primary School OFSTED report"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1238\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4194 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner.jpg 1920w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-300x193.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-1024x660.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-768x495.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-1536x990.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-310x200.jpg 310w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/04\/Linbury-banner-194x125.jpg 194w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1920px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1920\/1238;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>CCAC was intrigued to learn that our co-design collaboration with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.hassellstudio.com\/\">Xavier de Kestelier of Hassell<\/a> was mentioned in Coppermill Primary School\u2019s recent OFSTED report.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">CCAC was founded in 2020 by a small group of designers and educators who are committed to ensuring that both climate literacy and design should be properly represented in the primary curriculum. In this endeavour, we\u2019ve been helped by our courageous partner schools, who have embraced our programme and helped us to expand it. Coppermill has been a founding partner in this, and we expect to continue our collaboration in years to come.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The rewards for CCAC are manifold: but chiefly we value seeing the impact our work has on Yr 5 children \u2013 helping them to flourish, mature and begin to think about their future professional lives. To have this recognised by OFSTED is an added bonus.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>\u201cPupils take part in a wide variety of exciting activities which help them to understand the part they play in society\u2026They particularly enjoyed having the chance to work with an architect to design buildings for the future. Their work is displayed at a London gallery for others to learn from<\/em>.\u201d\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/files.ofsted.gov.uk\/v1\/file\/50252378\">Ofsted report, June 2024<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following Coppermill, Hassell has created a similar project at Clapham Manor Primary School and will start at St John\u2019s and St Clement\u2019s in the Autumn. CCAC sincerely appreciates Hassell\u2018s commitment to the programme and the inspiration their designers bring to London\u2019s primary school students.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Find out more about CCAC\u2019s <a href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/our-partners\/\">partner schools and designers here<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a id=\"_msocom_1\"><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Co-design collaboration with Xavier de Kestelier of Hassell was mentioned in Coppermill Primary School\u2019s recent OFSTED report<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":3